        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Task Template\n\nA task is a graph with one **goal**, its **work items** and its **open questions**.\n\nThe Detail, Summary and Glyph are not written by hand: the Method reads the graph and writes them, so the status is on every one of them. The views share one 3:2 shape, measured from their own width, and the glyph is the status.\n\nChange a work item's status and the views follow."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "task-template-derive-method",
      "type": "method",
      "label": "Derive the task views",
      "position": {
        "x": 160,
        "y": 1233
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "call",
          "key": "call",
          "label": "Call",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "key": "result",
          "label": "Result",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "call",
          "key": "call",
          "label": "Call",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180,
          "portId": "call"
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "key": "result",
          "label": "Result",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0,
          "portId": "result"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "scriptName": "Derive the task views",
        "parameters": [],
        "source": "// Derives the task's views from the task itself: nothing is typed into a summary.\n// It reads the goal, the work items (the tasks the goal contains) and the open questions, works out one status (Ready to confirm when all the work is done and the goal is not yet), and writes the Detail and Summary\n// views and the Glyph. It writes only those four, which its declared effects say.\nconst clean = (value) => String(value ?? '').trim();\nconst esc = (value) => clean(value)\n  .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/\"/g, '&quot;').replace(/'/g, '&#39;');\n\n// One status vocabulary, used at every size. `mark` is the Icon's symbol, `glyph` a Material icon name.\nconst STATUS = {\n  todo: { label: 'To do', mark: '○', glyph: 'RadioButtonUnchecked', ink: '#475569', tint: '#f1f5f9', line: '#cbd5e1' },\n  review: { label: 'Ready to confirm', mark: '◎', glyph: 'FactCheck', ink: '#6d28d9', tint: '#f5f3ff', line: '#ddd6fe' },\n  'in-progress': { label: 'In progress', mark: '▶', glyph: 'PlayCircleOutline', ink: '#1d4ed8', tint: '#eff6ff', line: '#bfdbfe' },\n  blocked: { label: 'Blocked', mark: '■', glyph: 'Block', ink: '#b91c1c', tint: '#fef2f2', line: '#fecaca' },\n  waiting: { label: 'Waiting', mark: '…', glyph: 'HourglassEmpty', ink: '#b45309', tint: '#fffbeb', line: '#fde68a' },\n  done: { label: 'Done', mark: '✓', glyph: 'CheckCircle', ink: '#15803d', tint: '#f0fdf4', line: '#bbf7d0' },\n  cancelled: { label: 'Cancelled', mark: '×', glyph: 'Cancel', ink: '#64748b', tint: '#f8fafc', line: '#e2e8f0' }\n};\nconst statusOf = (value) => (STATUS[clean(value)] ? clean(value) : 'todo');\nconst finished = (status) => status === 'done' || status === 'cancelled';\n\nconst nodes = await api.getNodes();\nconst edges = await api.getEdges();\nconst byId = new Map(nodes.map((node) => [node.id, node]));\nconst of = (type) => edges.filter((edge) => clean(edge.type) === type);\nconst titleOf = (node) => clean(node?.data?.title || node?.label);\n\n// The relationships say more than the status fields do. A decision that resolves a question answers it; something waiting on a\n// thing that is not resolved is blocked, whatever its own status field says; precedes puts work in order.\nconst isDecided = (node) => ['decided', 'accepted', 'done'].includes(clean(node?.data?.status));\n// A decision answers a question once it is decided, not while it is only proposed.\nconst resolvedByDecision = new Set(of('resolves').filter((edge) => isDecided(byId.get(edge.source))).map((edge) => edge.target));\nconst isResolved = (node) => {\n  if (!node) return true;\n  const own = clean(node.data?.status);\n  if (clean(node.type) === 'open-question') return own === 'answered' || resolvedByDecision.has(node.id);\n  if (clean(node.type) === 'decision') return isDecided(node);\n  return own === 'done' || own === 'cancelled';\n};\nconst blockersOf = (node) => of('blocked-by').filter((edge) => edge.source === node.id).map((edge) => byId.get(edge.target)).filter((target) => target && !isResolved(target));\n// Work is blocked when its own status says so, or when something it is blocked by is not yet resolved.\nconst stateOf = (node) => {\n  const own = statusOf(node.data?.status);\n  return !finished(own) && blockersOf(node).length ? 'blocked' : own;\n};\nconst reasonOf = (node) => clean(node.data?.blockedReason) || (blockersOf(node)[0] ? `Waiting on ${titleOf(blockersOf(node)[0])}` : '');\n\nconst goal = nodes.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'goal');\n// The task's work is what its goal contains. A task or a question that nothing contains is not counted: it shows under Needs you, so it is placed and not lost.\n// With no goal there is nothing to contain them, and every task counts.\nconst containedBy = (type) => new Set(of('contains').filter((edge) => goal && edge.source === goal.id).map((edge) => byId.get(edge.target)).filter((one) => one && clean(one.type) === type).map((one) => one.id));\nconst allTasks = nodes.filter((node) => clean(node.type) === 'task');\nconst inGoal = containedBy('task');\nconst bound = goal ? allTasks.filter((node) => inGoal.has(node.id)) : allTasks;\nconst unplacedTasks = goal ? allTasks.filter((node) => !inGoal.has(node.id)) : [];\n// In order: work that comes after other work (precedes) follows it.\nconst depthOf = (node, seen = new Set()) => {\n  if (seen.has(node.id)) return 0;\n  seen.add(node.id);\n  const before = of('precedes').filter((edge) => edge.target === node.id).map((edge) => byId.get(edge.source)).filter(Boolean);\n  return before.length ? 1 + Math.max(...before.map((one) => depthOf(one, new Set(seen)))) : 0;\n};\nconst items = bound.map((node, index) => ({ node, index, depth: depthOf(node) })).sort((x, y) => x.depth - y.depth || x.index - y.index).map(({ node }) => node);\nconst allQuestions = nodes.filter((node) => clean(node.type) === 'open-question');\nconst placedQuestions = new Set([...containedBy('open-question'), ...of('raises').filter((edge) => bound.some((one) => one.id === edge.source)).map((edge) => edge.target)]);\nconst questions = goal ? allQuestions.filter((node) => placedQuestions.has(node.id)) : allQuestions;\nconst strays = [...unplacedTasks, ...(goal ? allQuestions.filter((node) => !placedQuestions.has(node.id)) : [])];\nconst open = questions.filter((node) => !isResolved(node));\nconst counted = items.filter((node) => stateOf(node) !== 'cancelled');\nconst doneCount = counted.filter((node) => stateOf(node) === 'done').length;\nconst total = counted.length;\n\n// One status for the whole task.\nconst goalStatus = statusOf(goal?.data?.status);\nlet status;\nif (finished(goalStatus)) status = goalStatus;\nelse if (items.some((node) => stateOf(node) === 'blocked')) status = 'blocked';\nelse if (total && doneCount === total) status = 'review';\nelse if (items.some((node) => stateOf(node) === 'in-progress') || doneCount > 0) status = 'in-progress';\nelse if (items.some((node) => stateOf(node) === 'waiting')) status = 'waiting';\nelse status = 'todo';\nconst look = STATUS[status];\n\n// What happens next, or what is in the way.\nconst blocker = items.find((node) => stateOf(node) === 'blocked');\nconst readyToStart = (node) => of('precedes').filter((edge) => edge.target === node.id).every((edge) => isResolved(byId.get(edge.source)));\nconst live = items.find((node) => stateOf(node) === 'in-progress') || items.find((node) => stateOf(node) === 'todo' && readyToStart(node)) || items.find((node) => stateOf(node) === 'todo');\nconst next = status === 'blocked'\n  ? reasonOf(blocker) || `${titleOf(blocker)} is blocked`\n  : status === 'review' ? 'Confirm the goal is met' : status === 'done' || status === 'cancelled' ? '' : titleOf(live);\nconst title = titleOf(goal) || 'Untitled task';\nconst owner = clean(goal?.data?.owner);\nconst percent = total ? Math.round((doneCount / total) * 100) : 0;\nconst asked = open.length ? `${open.length} open question${open.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}` : 'No open questions';\n\nconst FONT = 'system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif';\n// The container is an outer wrapper and the page is inside it: a container's own padding and corners in cqw would otherwise be measured against the\n// window above it, not against the view.\nconst frame = (inner, extra = '') => `<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%;min-height:100%'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;font-family:${FONT};${extra}'>${inner}</div></div>`;\nconst chip = (state, size = 3.6) => {\n  const s = STATUS[state];\n  return `<span style='display:inline-block;padding:.3cqw 2.4cqw;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:${s.tint};color:${s.ink};border:1px solid ${s.line};font-weight:600;font-size:${size}cqw;line-height:1.4'>${esc(s.label)}</span>`;\n};\nconst bar = `<div style='height:1.8cqw;border-radius:1cqw;background:#e2e8f0;overflow:hidden'><div style='width:${percent}%;height:100%;background:${look.ink}'></div></div>`;\n\nconst summary = frame(\n  `<div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center'>${chip(status)}<span style='font-size:3.6cqw;color:#64748b'>${doneCount} of ${total}</span></div>`\n  + `<div style='font-weight:600;font-size:5.6cqw;line-height:1.2;color:#0f172a'>${esc(title)}</div>${bar}`\n  + (next ? `<div style='font-size:3.8cqw;line-height:1.3;color:${status === 'blocked' ? '#b91c1c' : '#334155'}'>${status === 'blocked' ? '' : 'Next: '}${esc(next)}</div>` : '')\n  + `<div style='margin-top:auto;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:3.4cqw;color:${open.length ? '#b45309' : '#64748b'}'><span>${esc(asked)}</span><span>${esc(owner)}</span></div>`,\n  `padding:5cqw 6cqw;border-radius:5cqw;background:#ffffff;border:1px solid ${status === 'blocked' ? look.line : '#e2e8f0'};display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2.6cqw`\n);\n\n\n// The Detail: one fixed page (3:2), so it fits its work instead of scrolling. A header, what needs the owner, three lanes of work, and what done\n// means. Heights are measured in cqw (the page is 66.7cqw tall). Each lane shows the cards that fit, at the density that shows the most, and says\n// how many more there are; the whole list is in the graph. (A scrollbar inside a graph view cannot be used with the mouse, so there is none.)\nconst PAGE = { height: 66.7, padding: 3.4, gap: 2.4, header: 9.5 };\nconst FIT = {\n  normal: { font: 3.5, pad: 1.6, gap: 1.6, wrap: true },\n  compact: { font: 2.9, pad: 1.0, gap: 1.0, wrap: false },\n  mini: { font: 2.5, pad: 0.6, gap: 0.8, wrap: false }\n};\nconst LANE_CHROME = 9.2;      // a lane's padding, its heading and the gap under it\nconst LANE_INNER = 25.3;      // the room a card has across, in cqw\nconst MORE_LINE = 3.6;\nconst cardHeight = (mode, titleLength) => {\n  const spec = FIT[mode];\n  const perLine = Math.max(4, Math.floor((LANE_INNER - spec.pad * 2 - 0.6) / (spec.font * 0.52) * 0.85));\n  const lines = spec.wrap ? Math.max(1, Math.ceil(titleLength / perLine)) : 1;\n  return lines * spec.font * 1.25 + spec.pad * 2 + 0.6;\n};\nconst card = (node, mode) => {\n  const state = stateOf(node);\n  const s = STATUS[state];\n  const spec = FIT[mode];\n  const edge = state === 'blocked' ? `border:1px solid ${s.line};background:${s.tint}` : state === 'in-progress' ? `border:1px solid ${s.line}` : 'border:1px solid #e2e8f0';\n  const nowrap = spec.wrap ? '' : ';white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis';\n  return `<div style='${edge};border-radius:2cqw;padding:${spec.pad}cqw ${spec.pad * 1.5}cqw;background:#ffffff;font-size:${spec.font}cqw;line-height:1.25;color:${finished(state) ? '#64748b' : '#0f172a'}${state === 'cancelled' ? ';text-decoration:line-through' : ''}${nowrap}'>${esc(node.data?.title || node.label)}</div>`;\n};\nconst inState = (...states) => items.filter((node) => states.includes(stateOf(node)));\n\n// What needs the owner: at most three lines, then how many more.\nconst wanted = [\n  ...items.filter((node) => stateOf(node) === 'blocked').map((node) => ({ mark: '■', text: `${clean(node.data?.title || node.label)}: ${reasonOf(node) || 'blocked'}` })),\n  ...(strays.length ? [{ mark: '↳', text: `${strays.length} not in this goal: ${strays.slice(0, 2).map((one) => clean(one.data?.title || one.label)).join(', ')}${strays.length > 2 ? '…' : ''}` }] : []),\n  ...open.map((node) => ({ mark: '?', text: clean(node.data?.title || node.label) }))\n];\n// What needs the owner: up to three lines under a heading; when the page is short, one row that holds the heading and the first item.\nconst needsHeightFor = (lines) => {\n  if (!wanted.length) return 0;\n  if (lines === 0) return 4.3 + 4.42;\n  const rows = 1 + lines;\n  return 4.3 + 4.42 * rows + 0.8 * (rows - 1);\n};\nconst needsFor = (lines) => {\n  if (!wanted.length) return '';\n  const row = (w) => `<div style='display:flex;gap:2cqw;min-width:0'><span>${w.mark}</span><span style='white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>${esc(w.text)}</span></div>`;\n  const box = 'border:1px solid #fecaca;background:#fef2f2;color:#b91c1c;border-radius:2.6cqw;padding:2cqw 2.8cqw;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.8cqw;font-size:3.4cqw;line-height:1.3';\n  const more = wanted.length - Math.max(1, lines);\n  if (lines === 0) {\n    return `<div style='${box}'><div style='display:flex;gap:2cqw;min-width:0'><span style='font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap'>Needs you${wanted.length > 1 ? ` · ${wanted.length}` : ''}</span><span style='white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>${wanted[0].mark} ${esc(wanted[0].text)}</span></div></div>`;\n  }\n  return `<div style='${box}'><div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between'><span style='font-weight:600'>Needs you</span>${more > 0 ? `<span style='opacity:.8'>+${more} more</span>` : ''}</div>${wanted.slice(0, lines).map(row).join('')}</div>`;\n};\n\nconst criteria = (Array.isArray(goal?.data?.successMetrics) ? goal.data.successMetrics : [])\n  .map((metric) => `<span>${status === 'done' ? '✓' : '○'} ${esc(metric)}</span>`);\nconst CRITERIA_HEIGHT = 3.6;\nconst ring = `<div style='width:9.5cqw;height:9.5cqw;border-radius:50%;background:conic-gradient(${look.ink} 0 ${percent}%,#e2e8f0 0);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex:none'><div style='width:7.2cqw;height:7.2cqw;border-radius:50%;background:#ffffff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:2.7cqw;font-weight:600;color:#0f172a'>${doneCount}/${total}</div></div>`;\n\n// The room the lanes have, and the cards that fit in it.\n// The page is budgeted so the lanes always have room: the header, then what needs the owner (up to three lines), then what done means (one line).\n// If the lanes would be left with too little, the Needs-you lines are cut back, then the criteria go, and the lanes keep at least this much.\nconst MIN_LANES = 26;\nconst titleLines = Math.min(2, Math.max(1, Math.ceil(title.length / 24)));\nconst headerHeight = Math.max(PAGE.header, titleLines * 5.5 + 3.8);\nlet needsLines = Math.min(wanted.length, 3);   // 0 means the one-row form\nlet showCriteria = criteria.length > 0;\nconst lanesFor = () => {\n  const sections = 2 + (wanted.length ? 1 : 0) + (showCriteria ? 1 : 0);\n  return PAGE.height - PAGE.padding * 2 - headerHeight - needsHeightFor(needsLines) - (showCriteria ? CRITERIA_HEIGHT : 0) - PAGE.gap * (sections - 1);\n};\nwhile (lanesFor() < MIN_LANES && needsLines > 0) needsLines -= 1;\nif (lanesFor() < MIN_LANES) showCriteria = false;\nconst needs = needsFor(needsLines);\nconst lanesHeight = lanesFor();\nconst room = lanesHeight - LANE_CHROME;\nconst laneLists = [inState('todo', 'waiting'), inState('in-progress', 'blocked'), inState('done', 'cancelled')];\nconst fitLane = (list, mode) => {\n  const spec = FIT[mode];\n  const heights = list.map((node) => cardHeight(mode, clean(node.data?.title || node.label).length) + spec.gap);\n  const all = heights.reduce((sum, h) => sum + h, 0);\n  if (all <= room) return list.length;\n  let used = 0; let shown = 0;\n  for (const h of heights) { if (used + h > room - MORE_LINE) break; used += h; shown += 1; }\n  return shown;\n};\nconst shownCount = (mode) => laneLists.reduce((sum, list) => sum + fitLane(list, mode), 0);\n// The density that shows the most cards; the larger one when they tie.\nconst mode = ['normal', 'compact', 'mini'].reduce((best, candidate) => (shownCount(candidate) > shownCount(best) ? candidate : best), 'normal');\nconst lane = (name, list, tone = '#64748b') => {\n  const shown = list.slice(0, fitLane(list, mode));\n  const more = list.length - shown.length;\n  return `<div style='background:#f8fafc;border-radius:2.6cqw;padding:2cqw;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:${FIT[mode].gap}cqw;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><div style='font-size:3cqw;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${tone};margin-bottom:.2cqw'>${name}${list.length ? ` · ${list.length}` : ''}</div>${shown.map((node) => card(node, mode)).join('')}${more ? `<div style='font-size:3cqw;color:#64748b'>+${more} more</div>` : ''}</div>`;\n};\nconst detail = frame(\n  `<div style='display:flex;align-items:center;gap:3cqw'>${ring}<div style='flex:1;min-width:0'><div style='font-weight:600;font-size:4.6cqw;line-height:1.2;color:#0f172a;display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden'>${esc(title)}</div><div style='font-size:3.2cqw;color:#64748b'>${esc(owner)}</div></div>${chip(status, 3.2)}</div>`\n  + needs\n  + `<div data-density='${mode}' style='display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:2cqw;flex:1;min-height:0;overflow:hidden'>${lane('Next', laneLists[0])}${lane('Doing', laneLists[1], '#1d4ed8')}${lane('Done', laneLists[2], '#15803d')}</div>`\n  + (showCriteria ? `<div style='font-size:3cqw;line-height:1.2;color:#64748b;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'><span style='font-weight:600'>Done when</span>  ${criteria.join('   ')}</div>` : ''),\n  'padding:3.4cqw 4cqw;border-radius:5cqw;background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2.4cqw;overflow:hidden'\n);\n\n\nconst faces = nodes.filter((node) => clean(node.type) === 'face');\nconst faceFor = (level) => faces.find((node) => clean(node.data?.semanticLevel) === level);\nconst glyph = nodes.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'glyph');\nfor (const [level, html] of [['detail', detail], ['summary', summary]]) {\n  const face = faceFor(level);\n  if (face) await api.updateView(face.id, { content: { kind: 'html', value: html } });\n}\nif (glyph) await api.updateNode(glyph.id, { data: { ...glyph.data, glyph: { kind: 'icon', name: look.glyph, color: look.ink } } });\nreturn { status, done: doneCount, total, open: open.length, next };\n",
        "effects": [
          {
            "kind": "update-node",
            "targets": [
              "task-template-detail",
              "task-template-summary",
              "task-template-glyph"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "allowMutations": true,
        "dryRun": false,
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "task-template-declaration"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793398056171,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
